# @zteam

When this rule is attached (`@zteam`) or the user says **zteam** / **/zteam** / **@zteam/…**:

## Subcommands

| Trigger | Do this |
|---------|---------|
| **`@zteam/config`** | Full setup: `get_zteam_config` → questions → `write_zteam_config`. See `.zteam/README.MD`. |
| **`@zteam/models`** | LLMs only: `get_zteam_config` → `modelQuestions` → `write_zteam_config` (update models in this project's `.zteam/config.json`). |
| **`@zteam/documentation`** | Config gate first, then `run_development_pipeline` with `workflow: "docs"`. |
| **`@zteam/tests`** | Config gate first, then QA-focused pipeline (`fix` / `feature` / `resume`). |
| **`@zteam`** (plain) | Config gate first, then full/auto pipeline. |

## Always

1. Call MCP on **`user-zteam`** (not Cursor Task subagents).
2. Pass **`workspaceRoot`** = absolute Cursor-open folder (required; MCP never uses sticky `mcp.json` `WORKSPACE_ROOT`).
3. Pass rich `userIdea` + **`projectRoot`** (prefer `samples/…`).
4. **Before any `run_development_pipeline`:** call **`get_zteam_config`**. If `needsConfig === true`, do **not** start the pipeline — run `@zteam/models` or `@zteam/config` (`write_zteam_config`) first, then re-check. Exceptions: `@zteam/config` / `@zteam/models` (they are the setup).
5. Report `workspaceRoot`, `appRoot`, `filesWritten`, `failureKind`, `resumeHint`; never silently copy sibling projects.
